  "equipment_type": "Sensor (humidity / temperature transmitter)",
  "applies_to": "Dwyer Series RHPX humidity and temperature transmitters with the BACnet MS/TP / Modbus RTU communication board, set to Modbus with DIP switch 9 (bulletin AQ-RHPX-C).",
  "summary": "The Dwyer RHPX is a duct or wall humidity and temperature transmitter that talks BACnet MS/TP or Modbus RTU on RS-485, chosen by DIP switch. Measurements are 32-bit floats in input registers: relative humidity, dew point, enthalpy and absolute humidity in two unit sets, and temperature. Offsets and display units are holding registers. This map covers every published register.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 127,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Tables list register numbers starting at 0001 and state that the register address is one less than the register number, so 0001-0002 (relative humidity) is read at address 0. Float registers 1-2000 are big-endian; the same values can be read with other byte orders by adding 2000 (byte swap), 4000 (word swap) or 6000 (little-endian)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Series RHPX Humidity/Temperature Communicating Transmitter - Specifications, Installation and Operating Instructions",
    "doc_number": "Bulletin AQ-RHPX-C",
    "revision_date": "2024-03",
    "url": "https://assets.dwyeromega.com/manuals-do/AQ_RHPX_C.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 4 (DIP switches, baud rates, function codes, input and holding register tables, error flags), p. 5 (multi-address byte-order table)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Byte order: addresses 1-2000 use big-endian order (ABCD for floats). Adding 2000 gives byte-swapped (BADC), 4000 word-swapped (CDAB) and 6000 little-endian (DCBA) copies; the info registers (8001+) exist only big-endian.",
    "Strings are read as a stream: first character in the high byte of the first register; unused bytes are zero.",
    "Holding register 0007-0023 Device name (String(32), default 'RHPX') is left out: the printed range spans 17 registers while a 32-character string needs 16.",
    "Supported functions: 03 (read holding), 04 (read input), 06 and 16.",
    "Default address 127 comes from the default DIP setting (switches 1-7 on). Baud, parity and stop bits are detected automatically ('Intelligent Serial Configuration'); supported: 9600-115200 baud, even/odd/none, 1 or 2 stop bits."
  ],
